<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Cosipa started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Brazil's Cosipa started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Bear Stearns said on Wednesday it had started coverage of Brazil's Companhia Siderurgica Paulista (Cosipa) with a rating of attractive.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Marco Soligo wrote in a report that Cosipa stock was cheap compared with fellow steel companies Usiminas, which controls Cosipa, and CSN.</p>
<p>-- &quot;While it (Cosipa) should post a loss this year and a much lower one in 1997, we expect profits from 1998 on.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's share was trading at 0.80 real in Sao Paulo.</p>
<p>-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879</p>
